GRAMMAR.md §3.1 rule 2 (log-2026-09-28 "check follow-ups 4 review", "round 3"): "??" cannot end a
line, so a field's type ending in "??" and a field on the next line need no separator: one
mistake ("T??" is not a type) does not also draw E1117. On one physical line it still does.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

record R {
  a: Int??
  b: Int
}

record S {
  a: Int?? b: Int
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E1117]  a/a.canon:9:12
  missing separator: put "," or a new line between items

1 error, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
